<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Hit Points</h1>
<p>Your hit points are your life. Damage takes them away, and you get them 
back slowly over time (see <a cmd='#'>Help Regenerate</a>), or faster with healing 
spells, potions and first aid. <a cmd='#'>score</a> shows how many you have of your 
most.
</p><p>How many you can have depends on your hit point ability (HPP), one of the 
abilities you raise as you train: your maximum is three times your HPP, 
plus 20. Your race and guild decide how easily it grows, and the spell 
raise hitpoints lifts it for a while. Your constitution decides how fast 
they come back. A character too old for their race has only 1.
</p><p>When your hit points run out, you go down and can't act:
</p>
<pre> 0 to -2     stunned: your hit points come back, and you get up
-3 to -5     incapacitated: you bleed, a hit point every half minute
-6 to -10    mortally wounded: you bleed faster, two every half minute
-11          dead
</pre>
<p>So once you are incapacitated, you die within about three minutes unless 
someone helps: first aid or a healing spell stops the bleeding by 
bringing you back up to stunned or better. The fight stops when you go 
down, but whoever was fighting you can still attack again and finish you 
off.
</p><p><br />
